            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
              <span style="font-size: 1.2rem;">⏳</span>
              <span style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-lufenia);">EX REVENGE</span>
            </div>
            <span class="badge-pill badge-crystal">
              <span class="psp-badge psp-shoulder" style="font-size: 0.7rem;">[ R ]</span> + <span class="psp-badge psp-square" style="font-size: 0.7rem;">🔲</span> (Hit)
            </span>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.6;">
            The ultimate defensive turnaround introduced in 012. Activated with a full EX Gauge while taking damage to shatter the enemy's combo!
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-sub); padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0.4rem 0 0 0; line-height: 1.55;">
            <li><strong>Time Dilation:</strong> Slows the opponent down to near-total paralysis while you move at normal speed.</li>
            <li><strong>Guaranteed Stagger:</strong> All your BRV attacks during Revenge ignore priority and guarantee unblockable wall rushes.</li>
            <li><strong>Meter Depletion:</strong> Drains your entire EX Gauge to 0 upon completion.</li>
            <li><strong>Finish on HP:</strong> Landing an HP attack during Revenge concludes the time freeze and deals massive HP damage.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 style="color: var(--color-ex-gauge); margin-top: 1.75rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
        <span>🎮</span> EX Burst Minigame Archetypes
      </h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.65;">
        When an EX Burst is triggered, an on-screen minigame determines the final damage multiplier:
      </p>

      <DataTable title="EX Burst Command Input Formats">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width: 180px;">Input Mechanism</th>
              <th style="width: 240px;">Character Roster Examples</th>
              <th>Minigame Execution & Success Tip</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {exBurstInputsTable.map(e => (
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
                    <span>{e.icon}</span>
                    <strong style="color: var(--color-ex-gauge);">{e.type}</strong>
                  </div>
                  <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;">
                    <span class={`psp-badge ${e.badgeInput}`}>{e.badgeLabel}</span>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub);">
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
                    {e.charImages.map(img => (
                      <img src={`${baseUrl}dissidia_012_characters/${img}`} alt="Character" style="width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border-panel); object-fit: cover;" />
                    ))}
                  </div>
                  <div>{e.characters}</div>
                </td>
                <td style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub);">
                  <div>{e.mechanic}</div>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </DataTable>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6: WALL RUSH & CHASE MECHANICS -->
  <section id="wall-rush-chase" class="guide-section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-title">
        <span class="badge-pill badge-cosmos">Stage Physics</span>
        <h2 style="margin: 0; border: none; padding: 0;">6. Wall Rush, Chases & Aerial Dynamics</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="crystal-panel">
      <p style="font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.65;">
        Stage geography is not merely cosmetic; positioning your opponent into physical collisions multiplies damage output and guarantees lethal combo strings.
      </p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div class="stat-panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--color-brv);">
          <h4 style="margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0; color: var(--color-brv); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
            <span>🧱</span> Wall Rush Damage Formula
          </h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.6;">
            When an attack with Wall Rush properties slams an opponent into a wall, ceiling, or floor, they take bonus collision damage equal to:
          </p>
          <div style="background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); padding: 0.5rem; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; color: #7dd3fc; margin: 0.5rem 0;">
            Wall Rush BRV = Target BRV × 0.125 to 0.25 (Modified by Sniper Eye / Muscle Belt)
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.84rem; color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 0;">
            Equipping accessories like <em>Sniper Eye</em> or <em>Muscle Belt</em> increases Wall Rush damage by up to +50%!
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--color-cosmos);">
          <h4 style="margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0; color: var(--color-cosmos); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
            <span>🎯</span> The Chase Sequence (RPS Dynamic)
          </h4>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.6;">
            Certain knockback attacks display a <span class="psp-badge psp-square">🔲 Square</span> prompt to initiate a high-speed Chase:
          </p>
          <ul style="font-size: 0.84rem; color: var(--text-sub); padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0.3rem 0 0 0; line-height: 1.5;">
            <li><strong>Attacker Options:</strong> BRV Attack (<span class="psp-badge psp-circle" style="font-size:0.7rem;">⭕</span>), HP Attack (<span class="psp-badge psp-square" style="font-size:0.7rem;">🔲</span>), or Feint / Cancel (<span class="psp-badge psp-cross" style="font-size:0.7rem;">✕</span>).</li>
            <li><strong>Defender Options:</strong> Dodge (<span class="psp-badge psp-cross" style="font-size:0.7rem;">✕</span>) to evade, Guard (<span class="psp-badge psp-shoulder" style="font-size:0.7rem;">[ R ]</span>) to deflect BRV attacks, or predict HP strike.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7: DAMAGE FORMULAS & FRAME CANCELING -->
  <section id="damage-cancels" class="guide-section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-title">
        <span class="badge-pill badge-cosmos">Calculations</span>
        <h2 style="margin: 0; border: none; padding: 0;">7. Damage Calculations, Multipliers & Frame Canceling</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="crystal-panel">
      <h3 style="color: var(--color-brv); margin-top: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
        <span>📐</span> Mathematical Damage Formula
      </h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.94rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.65;">
        Every point of Bravery dealt in battle is calculated according to the master damage equation:
      </p>

      <div style="background: var(--surface-panel-alt); border: 1px solid var(--border-panel); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); margin: 1.25rem 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.92rem; color: #bae6fd; overflow-x: auto;">
        BRV Damage = ⌊ (Attacker ATK - Defender DEF + 100) × (Move Power / 100) × ∏(Booster Multipliers) × Crit Multiplier ⌋
      </div>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div class="stat-panel">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">
            <span>⚡</span>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-brv); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;">Critical Hit Multipliers</div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 700; color: #fff;">1.5× to 2.0× Base Damage</div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 0.2rem;">Triggered on Backstabs, Counter-Attacks, or automatically when the target is Broken.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-panel">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">
            <span>✖️</span>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-cosmos); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;">Booster Stacking Formula</div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 700; color: #fff;">Multiplicative (∏)</div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 0.2rem;">Boosters multiply together (e.g., 1.5 × 1.5 × 1.4 = 3.15× total modifier).</div>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-panel">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">
            <span>🛡️</span>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--color-hp); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;">Damage Floor & Cap</div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 700; color: #fff;">1 Min / 9,999 Max</div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-dim); margin-top: 0.2rem;">A single hit cannot deal less than 1 or exceed 9,999 without special artifact uncap gear.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 style="color: var(--color-brv); margin-top: 2rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
        <span>⏩</span> Advanced Frame Canceling Techniques
      </h3>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-sub); font-size: 0.92rem; padding-left: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <li><strong>Dodge Canceling (DC):</strong> Inputting a dodge immediately upon the final hit connecting cancels the ending lag frames of a move (essential on Squall's <em>Solid Barrel</em>, Cloud's <em>Slashing Blow</em>, and Lightning's <em>Rush Assault</em>).</li>
        <li><strong>Jump Canceling (JC):</strong> Tapping jump during the recovery of grounded launcher attacks transitions the fighter directly into aerial combo strings without delay.</li>
        <li><strong>Paradigm Shift / Weapon Switch Canceling:</strong> Lightning's <span class="psp-badge psp-shoulder">[ L ]</span> + <span class="psp-badge psp-shoulder">[ R ]</span> Optima Shift and Vaan's weapon switch cancel active attack recovery animations into immediate defensive guards or followup strikes.</li>
        <li><strong>Branching Attacks / Link Abilities:</strong> Upgrading core BRV moves with AP unlocks direct branching into HP finishers (e.g. Cloud's <em>Slashing Blow &rarr; Omnislash v5</em>, Squall's <em>Heel Drop &rarr; Revolver Drive</em>, Bartz's <em>Slide Shock &rarr; HP Blast</em>).</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 8: SUMMONS & COUNTER-PLAY -->
  <section id="summon-tactics" class="guide-section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-title">
        <span class="badge-pill badge-cosmos">Summon Stones</span>
        <h2 style="margin: 0; border: none; padding: 0;">8. Summon System & Strategic Counter-Play</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="crystal-panel">
      <p style="font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.65;">
        Summon Stones are equippable battle augments that execute game-altering effects. Summons are divided into <strong>Auto Summons</strong> (trigger automatically when specific battle conditions are met) and <strong>Manual Summons</strong> (activated on demand with <span class="psp-badge psp-shoulder">[ R ]</span> + <span class="psp-badge psp-square">🔲</span> + <span class="psp-badge psp-triangle">▲</span>).
      </p>

      <DataTable title="Summon Classifications & Matchup Roles">
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="width: 180px;">Category</th>
              <th style="width: 190px;">Notable Summons</th>
              <th>Mechanical Effect</th>
              <th>Competitive Counter-Play Application</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {summonClassifications.map(s => (
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem;">
                    <span>{s.icon}</span>
                    <strong style="color: var(--color-lufenia);">{s.category}</strong>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub);">{s.summons}</td>
                <td style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub);">{s.effect}</td>
                <td style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-dim);">{s.tactic}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </DataTable>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 9: EQUIPMENT SYNERGY & BUILDS -->
  <section id="build-archetypes" class="guide-section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-title">
        <span class="badge-pill badge-cosmos">Metagame</span>
        <h2 style="margin: 0; border: none; padding: 0;">9. Equipment Synergy & Competitive Build Archetypes</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="crystal-panel">
      <p style="font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.65;">
        Endgame and competitive Dissidia 012 builds maximize performance through <strong>Booster Accessory Stacking</strong>. Equipping 1-2 core accessories alongside 6-7 high-multiplier condition boosters can elevate damage output by <strong>500% to 1500%</strong>.
      </p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <!-- BUILD 1: INITIAL ASSIST (IA) META -->
        <div class="stat-panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--color-assist);">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
            <span>⚡</span>
            <div style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-assist);">
              1. Initial Assist (IA) Meta
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
            Core: Together as One, Side by Side, Assist Boosters
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            Starts the battle with 1-2 full Assist bars. Allows immediate first-contact Assist calls (Kuja/Jecht) to confirm instant round-opening HP conversions and lock down aggressive rushdown fighters.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- BUILD 2: EX REVENGE / DURATION META -->
        <div class="stat-panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--color-ex-gauge);">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
            <span>🌟</span>
            <div style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-ex-gauge);">
              2. Pure EX / Revenge Dominance
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
            Core: Center of the World, Pearl Necklace, Dragonfly Saint
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            Maximizes EX Force suction radius and EX Core absorption. Guarantees permanent EX Revenge availability as an impenetrable safety net while maintaining high HP Regen in EX Mode.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- BUILD 3: WALL RUSH SPIKE BUILD -->
        <div class="stat-panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--color-brv);">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
            <span>💥</span>
            <div style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-brv);">
              3. Wall Rush Heavy Artillery
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
            Core: Sniper Eye, Muscle Belt, Airborne / Ground Boosters
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            Stacks Wall Rush bonus damage multipliers to strip 50%+ of the opponent's Bravery on every single wall collision. Devastating on enclosed stages like Planet's Core and Pandaemonium.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- BUILD 4: ANTI-BOSS 000 SURVIVAL -->
        <div class="stat-panel" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--color-chaos);">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
            <span>🛡️</span>
            <div style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-chaos);">
              4. Level 130 Boss Survival Setup
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">
            Core: Safety Bit, First Aid, EXP to HP, Auto-Phoenix
          </div>
          <p style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-sub); line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
            Specifically tuned to withstand Level 130 Feral Chaos and Gateway 000 super-bosses. Prevents one-shot Break kills and converts battle EXP directly into survival HP recovery.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
